       _f_d is the file descriptor to associate with the XRCD.  _o_f_l_a_g  describes
       the desired creation attributes.  It is a bitwise OR of zero or more of
       the following flags:

       OO__CCRREEAATT
              Indicates that an XRCD should be created and associated with the
              inode referenced by the given fd.  If the XRCD exists, this flag
              has no effect except as noted under OO__EEXXCCLL below.

       OO__EEXXCCLL If OO__EEXXCCLL and OO__CCRREEAATT are set, open will fail if an XRCD associ‐
              ated with the inode exists.

       If _f_d equals -1, no inode is associated with the XRCD. To indicate that
       XRCD should be created, use _o_f_l_a_g = OO__CCRREEAATT.

       iibbvv__cclloossee__xxrrccdd(()) closes the XRCD _x_r_c_d.  If this is the last  reference,
       the XRCD will be destroyed.

